  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the child as a representation of perceived immaturity in the context of gender identity choices",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the child (child), who is used as a symbol for perceived immaturity and lack of agency in making basic life decisions. This projection is implicit, as the meme uses the child's image to contrast with the text about gender identity, suggesting that the user (or the audience) should see the child as embodying the 'immature' perspective being mocked. The projection is not explicit with deictic pronouns like 'you' or 'me', but it is implied through the framing of the child as the subject of the comparison, making the user identify with the perspective of the child or the judgment being made about the child's 'maturity'.",
  "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface",
